OL,3,CSolar eclipse: Your questions answered
OL,5,FThe Sun may appear dimmer, making it
OL,6,Feasier to look at than usual, but
OL,7,Fthere is still harmful solar radiation
OL,8,Fwhich can damage your retina without
OL,9,Fcausing any pain, meaning people may
OL,10,Fnot realise there is a problem until
OL,11,Fafterwards.
OL,13,FEclipse glasses
OL,15,FNormal sunglasses are not strong
OL,16,Fenough, but you can watch it through
OL,17,Fcertified eclipse glasses, or handheld
OL,18,Fsolar viewers - with experts advising
OL,19,Fthat they must meet the international
OL,20,Fsafety standard ISO 12312-2.
OL,1,W~+$z5~{4~k4~k4~sj5  hws         G5/7
OL,2,W+.!/*%/*%/*%/*%+,"-$ /(,'T(,,,,,,,,,,,,
