OL,3,CSolar eclipse: Your questions answered
OL,5,FThe eclipse can be seen in the
OL,6,Freflected image as the Moon starts to
OL,7,Ftake a "bite" out of the Sun,
OL,8,Fappearing upside down compared with
OL,9,Fits position in the sky. If clouds
OL,10,Fmove across the face of the Sun, they
OL,11,Fcan be seen as well.
OL,13,FDo not look into the mirror during the
OL,14,Feclipse, as this is just as dangerous
OL,15,Fas looking directly at the Sun.
OL,17,FOther advice can be found on the Royal
OL,18,FMuseums Greenwich website.
OL,1,W~+$z5~{4~k4~k4~sj5  hws         G7/7
